# 📐 CO-PILOT PAGE ORGANIZATION STRATEGY
## How to Fit All New Capabilities on Co-Pilot Pages

**Created:** 2024-12-19  
**Status:** 🟡 PLANNING - Addressing Page Organization  
**Problem:** Adding 6-8 new capabilities across co-pilots - need strategy to prevent page bloat

---

## 🎯 THE CHALLENGE

### **Current State:**
- Co-pilots typically have **3-5 capabilities**
- Uses **tabbed interface** showing one capability at a time
- Capabilities rendered in `TacticalCapabilityMatrix` component

### **After Phase 2:**
- **Clinical co-pilots** (5 files): +1 capability (Integrated Care) = **4-6 total**
- **Therapy Fit:** +2 capabilities (Integrated Care + Synthetic Lethality) = **5-7 total**
- **Pathway:** +3 capabilities (Integrated Care + Synthetic Lethality + Gene Essentiality) = **6-8 total**
- **Chemo:** +2 capabilities (Integrated Care + Gene Essentiality) = **5-7 total**
- **CRISPR:** +3 capabilities (Integrated Care + IND Package + IP Monetization) = **6-8 total**

**Risk:** Too many tabs = cluttered UI, overwhelming user experience

---

## 📋 ORGANIZATION STRATEGIES

### **STRATEGY 1: PRIORITIZED GROUPING** ⭐ RECOMMENDED

**Concept:** Group capabilities into "Core" and "Advanced" sections

**Implementation:**
- **Core Capabilities** (always visible): 3-4 primary capabilities
- **Advanced Features** (collapsed section): Additional capabilities grouped together

**Example Structure:**
```typescript
keyCapabilities: [
  // CORE CAPABILITIES (Primary tab interface)
  { title: "Biology-Aware Drug Ranking", ... }, // Existing
  { title: "Biomarkers & Cohort Context", ... }, // Existing
  { title: "Synthetic Lethality Analysis", ... }, // New
  
  // ADVANCED FEATURES (Grouped section)
  {
    title: "Advanced Features",
    isGroup: true,
    capabilities: [
      { title: "Integrated Care Plan", ... }, // New
      { title: "Gene Essentiality Scoring", ... }, // New (if applicable)
    ]
  }
]
```

**Pros:**
- ✅ Keeps primary tabs focused (3-4 tabs)
- ✅ Advanced features discoverable but not overwhelming
- ✅ Maintains clean UI

**Cons:**
- ⚠️ Requires component modification to handle grouped capabilities

---

### **STRATEGY 2: COLLAPSIBLE "MORE FEATURES" SECTION** ⭐ ALTERNATIVE

**Concept:** Add a separate section below capability tabs for additional features

**Implementation:**
```typescript
// In co-pilot data structure
keyCapabilities: [
  // Primary capabilities (shown in tabs)
  { title: "Biology-Aware Drug Ranking", ... },
  { title: "Biomarkers & Cohort Context", ... },
  { title: "Synthetic Lethality Analysis", ... },
],

// New section for additional features
additionalFeatures: [
  { title: "Integrated Care Plan", ... },
  { title: "Gene Essentiality Scoring", ... },
]
```

**Rendering:**
- Primary capabilities → Tabbed interface (as-is)
- Additional features → Collapsible "More Features" section below

**Pros:**
- ✅ No component changes needed for tab interface
- ✅ Clear separation of primary vs. additional
- ✅ Easy to expand/collapse

**Cons:**
- ⚠️ Requires new data structure field
- ⚠️ Requires new component section

---

### **STRATEGY 3: SMART TAB GROUPING** ⭐ BEST UX

**Concept:** Group related capabilities under unified tabs

**Implementation:**
```typescript
keyCapabilities: [
  {
    title: "Therapeutic Intelligence",
    groupCapabilities: [
      { title: "Biology-Aware Drug Ranking", ... },
      { title: "Synthetic Lethality Analysis", ... },
      { title: "Gene Essentiality Scoring", ... },
    ]
  },
  {
    title: "Integrated Care",
    groupCapabilities: [
      { title: "Complete Care Plan", ... },
    ]
  },
  {
    title: "Biomarkers & Context",
    groupCapabilities: [
      { title: "Biomarkers & Cohort Context", ... },
    ]
  }
]
```

**Rendering:**
- Tab shows group title
- Inside tab, show sub-tabs for individual capabilities
- Nested tab interface

**Pros:**
- ✅ Logical grouping
- ✅ Cleaner top-level tabs
- ✅ Related capabilities together

**Cons:**
- ⚠️ Requires significant component refactoring
- ⚠️ Nested tabs add complexity

---

### **STRATEGY 4: PRIORITIZATION + SHOW MORE** ⭐ SIMPLEST

**Concept:** Keep all capabilities in tabs, but prioritize and add "Show All" toggle

**Implementation:**
- **Default:** Show 3-4 primary capabilities in tabs
- **"Show All Capabilities"** toggle → Expands to show all 6-8 capabilities
- Prioritize by: Core functionality first, Advanced features last

**Pros:**
- ✅ Minimal code changes
- ✅ Progressive disclosure
- ✅ Maintains existing structure

**Cons:**
- ⚠️ More tabs visible when expanded

---

## 🎯 RECOMMENDED APPROACH: HYBRID STRATEGY

### **Combining Strategy 1 + Strategy 4:**

1. **Primary Capabilities** (Always Visible): 3-4 core capabilities in tabs
2. **Integrated Care** (Always Last): Separate "Integrated Care Plan" section below capability tabs
3. **Advanced Features** (Collapsed): Additional capabilities in collapsible section

**Structure:**
```typescript
// Co-pilot data structure
keyCapabilities: [
  // PRIMARY CAPABILITIES (Core tabbed interface)
  { title: "Biology-Aware Drug Ranking", priority: "primary", ... },
  { title: "Biomarkers & Cohort Context", priority: "primary", ... },
  { title: "Synthetic Lethality Analysis", priority: "primary", ... },
  
  // ADVANCED CAPABILITIES (Collapsed by default)
  { title: "Gene Essentiality Scoring", priority: "advanced", ... },
],

// INTEGRATED CARE (Separate section - always visible but at bottom)
integratedCare: {
  title: "Integrated Care Plan",
  description: "...",
  // Full KeyCapability structure
}
```

**Rendering Order:**
1. **Hero Section** (existing)
2. **Primary Capabilities** (tabbed interface, 3-4 tabs)
3. **Advanced Features** (collapsible section with 1-2 capabilities)
4. **Integrated Care Plan** (prominent section at bottom)
5. **Value Propositions** (existing)
6. **Conclusion** (existing)

