## 🎨 UI/UX DESIGN

### **Primary Capabilities Section**
- **Location:** Standard tabbed interface (existing)
- **Tabs:** 3-4 tabs maximum
- **Style:** Existing design, no changes

### **Advanced Features Section**
- **Location:** Below primary capabilities
- **Design:** Collapsible card with "Advanced Features" header
- **Default State:** Collapsed (shows count: "2 advanced features")
- **Expanded State:** Shows capabilities in compact cards or sub-tabs

```tsx
<AdvancedFeaturesSection>
  <CollapsibleCard>
    <Header>
      <h3>Advanced Features</h3>
      <Badge>2 capabilities</Badge>
      <ExpandIcon />
    </Header>
    <Content>
      {/* Show capabilities in compact cards or sub-tabs */}
    </Content>
  </CollapsibleCard>
</AdvancedFeaturesSection>
```

### **Integrated Care Section**
- **Location:** Below all capabilities, before Value Propositions
- **Design:** Prominent card/section with distinct styling
- **Purpose:** Highlight integration with Unified Care Plan
- **Style:** Slightly larger, highlighted border, distinct background

```tsx
<IntegratedCareSection>
  <ProminentCard className="border-2 border-blue-500 bg-blue-50">
    <Header>
      <Icon>Network</Icon>
      <h2>Integrated Care Plan</h2>
      <Badge>All Capabilities Unified</Badge>
    </Header>
    {/* Full KeyCapabilityDisplay */}
  </ProminentCard>
</IntegratedCareSection>
```

